+// Pinned version of [`punktfunk_probe`]: offers punktfunk/2 first (and punktfunk/1 for older
+// hosts), verifies the host leaf against `pin_sha256` (null = trust on first use), and returns
+// [`PUNKTFUNK_STATUS_CRYPTO`] on a mismatch while still writing the presented fingerprint to
+// `observed_sha256_out`. `PUNKTFUNK_STATUS_TIMEOUT` when nothing answered. Blocks up to
+// `timeout_ms`; run it off the UI thread.
+//
+// # Safety
+// `host` is a NUL-terminated UTF-8 string; `pin_sha256` is null or readable for 32 bytes;
+// `observed_sha256_out` is null, or writable for 32 bytes.
+PunktfunkStatus punktfunk_probe_ex(const char *host,
+                                   uint16_t port,
+                                   const uint8_t *pin_sha256,
+                                   uint32_t timeout_ms,
